d style=\\\"font-family: Verdana; font-size: 10px; padding: 15px 15px;\\\">(NOTE: ONLY APPLICABLE IF THE FLASH AND BATT SYSTEM IS APPLIED IN EXTERIOR WALLS)<br>The 'Flash and Batt&middot; procedure is not recommended or approved by any of the Spray Foam or Fiberglass Insulation Manufacturers. Modern building science also does not support installing a \\\"Flash and Batt&bull; system in a wall cavity if less than 2&middot; of closed cell spray foam is installed. Ignoring these recommendations and this science greatly increases the risk of condensation forming on the interior side of the spray foam within the wall cavity, which condensation can cause permanent and significant damage to the building, its components, and occupants. The \\\"Flash and Batt\\\" process requires the installation of a minimum of 2&bull; of closed cell spray foam in all \\\"Flash and Batt' applications, regardless of wall cavity depth. If you specify that we do not follow that process and that we instead install less than 2&bull; of closed cell spray foam in your wall cavity, we ask that you acknowledge, by your signature, that you have read and understand the risks described above. You forever release Goley Inc. and its employees and agents from any and all claims and demands arising from or related to the insulation procedure described above and hold Goley Inc. harmless and free of all culpability should your wall system fail at any time and in any way as a result of the procedure requested by you. By accepting this Proposal in whole or in part you acknowledge receipt of the above information.</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr style=\\\"height: 247.539px;\\\">\\n<td style=\\\"width: 99.7059%;\\\">\\n<table style=\\\"font-size: 16px; background-color: #000000;\\\" border=\\\"0\\\" width=\\\"100%\\\" cellspacing=\\\"0\\\" cellpadding=\\\"2\\\">\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style